    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d553">

                <pb facs="0478" n="362" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg362"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/1039.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Minister Blanchard.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-28T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 28, 1914, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your November 25, 3 p.m. You may inform Theodore that the Department is ready to
                    use its good offices with the Bank to secure, first, a small loan to cover
                    legitimate traveling expenses of the commission; second, as soon as you report
                    that the credentials of the commission are satisfactory, a further loan to take
                    care of the running expenses of the Government during the time that the
                    commission is in session.</p>
                <p>Department’s November 24, 5 p.m., was drafted to prevent any possibility of bad
                    faith on the part of Théodore.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
